- With remote control you can manage a running personalDNSfilter instance remotely from the Android App.
- Useful especially when running the desktop/headless version without UI.
- On the remote server you want to manage, enable this feature in dnsfilter.conf by setting:
  ==> server_remote_ctrl_port = 3333
  ==> server_remote_ctrl_keyphrase = <a strong shared secret keyphrase>
- Wait/restart the remote instance so the listener starts. (A non-empty keyphrase is required.)
- On the Android client you want to use for remote control, configure:
  ==> client_remote_ctrl_host = <IP address or hostname of the remote server>
  ==> client_remote_ctrl_port = 3333
  ==> client_remote_ctrl_keyphrase = <matching shared secret keyphrase>
- Restart or reconnect from the Android UI using the remote control option.
